Nrityapath AI

AI-powered Bharatanatyam movement & storytelling notation generator

Live Prototype  
https://bharatanatyam-notati-9g3s.bolt.host

Nrityapath uses AI to convert movement descriptions or narrative stories into structured Bharatanatyam choreography notation — complete with posture glyphs, mudras, beats, expression cues, and teaching notes.

It introduces a new, lightweight digital notation standard for classical Indian dance:
NNF — Nrityapath Notation Format

Built during the AI Genesis Hackathon (Nov 2025) using Gemini + Opus + a custom visual prototype.

⸻

Why Nrityapath?

Bharatanatyam has survived for 2,000 years through oral, visual, and embodied teaching.
But today, it still has no universal digital notation system.

This creates major gaps:
	•	Students forget sequences
	•	Teachers rely on memory instead of documentation
	•	Learners outside India struggle to stay consistent
	•	Choreography cannot be archived or shared properly

Nrityapath bridges tradition and technology by converting text → structured choreography → visual steps.

⸻

What Nrityapath Does

Nrityapath generates structured dance notation in two modes:

1. Movement → Notation

Short phrases describing posture, mudra, direction, and beats. Example: “araimandi, alapadma, step forward for 2 beats.”

2. Story → Notation

Narratives describing characters, scenarios, or emotional expressions. Prompts like: “A devotee walks toward a temple with light karuna rasa.”

Both modes output standardized JSON following the NNF schema.

⸻

Who Is It For?

Primary Users
	•	Dancers (beginner ↔ advanced)
	•	Choreographers
	•	Students learning adavus / abhinaya

Secondary Users
	•	Teachers and academies
	•	Digital archivists & cultural institutions
	•	Designers/developers building dance-tech tools
	•	Anyone who prefers structured visual learning

⸻

Key Features

✔ Natural Language → NNF JSON

Every prompt is transformed into a structured sequence with:
	•	Posture (ARA, SAM, MND)
	•	Mudra (ALA, KAT, PTA, TRI…)
	•	Movement type (FWD, TURN_R, STATIC…)
	•	Beats (1B, 2B, 4B)
	•	Direction
	•	Rasa expression
	•	Teaching notes

✔ Story → Choreography

Narratives become expressive step sequences.

✔ Visual Renderer (Prototype UI)

Shows:
	•	Stick-figure poses
	•	Mudra & posture icons
	•	Direction arrows
	•	Beat markers
	•	Teaching notes
	•	Step navigation

✔ Opus Workflow Integration

Every generation passes through:
	•	Input intake
	•	NNF Generator (Gemini)
	•	Rule-checking (schema validation)
	•	Agentic Review
	•	Human Review
	•	Audit summary
	•	Clean, final JSON output

⸻

NNF — Nrityapath Notation Format

Full specification lives here:
nnf_schema.md

Simplified Output Structure

{
  "mode": "movement",
  "level": "beginner",
  "rasa": "none",
  "steps": [
      { /* step object */ }
  ]
}

