Featured Example (Fully Visualized)

Only one sequence is currently fully illustrated in the live prototype:

Beginner – Mandi Adavu (Year 2 – Adavu 1)

File: movement_mandi_adavu_beginner.json
This is the sequence used in the Framer/Bolt UI with four custom stick-figure images.

All other examples exist as JSON for future expansion.


Sample Output (short)

{
  "mode": "movement",
  "level": "beginner",
  "rasa": "none",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "posture": "ARA",
      "hand_mudra": "ALA",
      "movement": "TURN_R",
      "beats": "1B",
      "direction": "RIGHT",
      "description": "Execute a controlled pivot to face the right side.",
      "rasa_expression": "none",
      "teaching_note": "Keep the center of gravity low and steady."
    }
  ]
}

More examples are in /examples.

⸻

How it Works

1. Gemini / Google AI Studio
	•	System prompt enforces strict NNF format
	•	User input → validated JSON
	•	Tested with 14 prompts (movement + story)
	•	Ensures predictable outputs for Opus + Framer

2. Opus Workflow

Public Template

https://app.opus.com/app/workflow/share/30455570-d049-4e60-90f2-e1a600f6885a

Includes:
	•	Input intake
	•	NNF Generator (LLM agent)
	•	Rule checks (valid codes, structure)
	•	Agentic Review (safety + schema adherence)
	•	Human Review (culture-checked + corrections)
	•	Audit Node (JSON summary with timestamps & actions)
	•	Delivery Node (final clean output)

Satisfies All Hackathon Requirements:
	•	data import
	•	deterministic + AI reasoning
	•	routing & exception handling
	•	two review layers
	•	traceable audit artifact
	•	export ready

3. Framer Prototype (Visual Renderer)

Coming next.

Will display:
	•	Stick figure per step
	•	Mudra icons
	•	Direction arrows
	•	Beat timing
	•	Rasa expressions
	•	Teaching notes
	•	Step-by-step flow animation

Perfect for demo & judging.

⸻

Why Nrityapath Matters

Classical dance has:
	•	Structured grammar
	•	Codified mudras
	•	Defined postures
	•	Formal rasas
But no modern notation standard.

Nrityapath proposes:
	•	A new digital language for Bharatanatyam
	•	AI-assisted choreography creation
	•	Culturally consistent outputs
	•	Archival possibilities
	•	Global accessibility

⸻

Tech Stack:
	•	Chat-GPT (prompting)
	•	Gemini (generation)
	•	Opus (workflow automation, review, audit)
	•	Framer / Bolt.new (UI visualization)
	•	GitHub — schema + examples + documentation

⸻

Setup for Developers

No backend needed.

To test:
	1.	Open Framer
	2.	Paste any JSON from /examples
	3.	View instant choreography visualization

Optional: integrate Gemini API + Opus workflow.

